---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Stamp from '../../components/Stamp.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Photo & Artwork Consent Policy"
  description="How CREATE & CARE protects workshop participants' privacy and enforces written photo and artwork consent before publishing."
>
  <section class="page-hero band-rose">
    <div class="container page-hero-inner">
      <Stamp text="PARTICIPANT DIGNITY & WRITTEN CONSENT" variant="brick" rotate={-1} />
      <h1>Photo &amp; Artwork Consent Policy</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Taking part in a CREATE &amp; CARE workshop never requires you to appear in a photograph or publish your artwork online.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-band band-paper">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="legal-card prose">
        <h2>Our Golden Rule for Workshop Photos</h2>
        <p>
          We only publish photographs showing identifiable people—or personal artworks created during workshops—when the participant has signed a clear, voluntary written consent form. Taking part in any workshop, online hub or local exhibition is completely independent of photo consent.
        </p>

        <h2>Technical Safeguard on This Website</h2>
        <p>
          Our website build pipeline automatically checks every news post and event before publishing. If an editor attaches an image file without setting `consent: true` in the article metadata, the build fails and the photo cannot be deployed to `createandcare.eu`.
        </p>

        <h2>Withdrawing Consent &amp; Removal Requests</h2>
        <p>
          Participants can withdraw their consent for a photograph or artwork at any time without giving a reason. Upon request, we remove the image immediately from this website, social media channels and the Artsteps VR gallery.
        </p>
        <p><code class="placeholder-tag">[TO BE COMPLETED BY INTEGRATIONAL e.V.]</code></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-card {
    background-color: var(--paper);
    border: var(--border-thick);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-hard);
  }
</style>
